Touching this file starts a snipe run.

GitHub's scheduler has not fired a single run of the 15-minute watch since it
was armed, while push-triggered runs work every time. Since the whole project
comes down to two moments that do not repeat, this exists so those moments do
not depend on a scheduler that has yet to prove itself.

The snipe script waits out the remaining time itself, so firing it any time in
the half hour before a release works.

fired: never
